---
// The gap — deck slide 3 rebuilt as two app-icon rows. Row one is true
// today: a check tile and "Anyone can build an app." Row two arrives false:
// an X tile and a struck, muted "Anyone can acquire users." As the row
// scrolls up the page the tile flips over, X on the back, the Ube [u] icon
// on the front, and the strike erases; scrolling back reverses it. The
// sentence turns true because Ube stepped in front of it. The short line
// below names the change: growing an app becomes as easy as building one.
//
// Motion is CSS scroll-driven (a named view timeline on row two, no JS).
// Without support (Firefox, older Safari) or with reduced motion, the row
// renders its finished state: Ube icon, no strike. The eyebrow and closing
// line carry the argument on their own.
//
// The tiles are built in markup and CSS, not the PNG, so they track the
// accent token. Geometry is measured off public/assets/favicons/logo-512.png
// (512 grid, in fractions of the tile side): brackets 69 wide x 380 tall,
// 49.5 stroke, inset 56 from the sides and 66 from the top; the "u" has a
// 206 x-height. Brackets are built like Wordmark.astro's (open box, square
// corners), only thicker, as in the icon. At text size the icon's own
// margins read cramped, so `.gap-glyph` shrinks brackets + "u" inside the
// tile without touching that geometry.
//
// The visual rows are aria-hidden. The heading's accessible name is the
// truthful sentence, so a screen reader never hears the struck line, or
// the turned line, as a claim about today. The build/acquire rows are deck
// slide 3; the closing line is slide 14 (as building gets easier,
// distribution becomes the bottleneck).
---

<section class="about-gap" aria-labelledby="about-gap-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow">Our goal</div>

    <div class="gap-statement">
      <h2 class="gap-title" id="about-gap-title">
        <span class="sr-only">
          Anyone can build an app. Not everyone can acquire users yet.
        </span>{" "}
        <span class="gap-rows" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="gap-row">
            <span class="gap-tile gap-face">
              <span class="gap-check"></span>
            </span>
            <span class="gap-line"
              >Anyone can<br class="gap-br" /> build an app.</span
            >
          </span>{" "}
          <span class="gap-row gap-row-turn">
            <span class="gap-tile gap-flip">
              <span class="gap-face gap-face-x">
                <span class="gap-x"></span>
              </span>
              <span class="gap-face gap-face-ube">
                <span class="gap-glyph">
                  <span class="gap-bracket gap-bracket-l"></span>
                  <span class="gap-u"></span>
                  <span class="gap-bracket gap-bracket-r"></span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="gap-line">
              <span class="gap-strike"
                >Anyone can<br class="gap-br" /> acquire users.</span
              >
            </span>
          </span>
        </span>
      </h2>

      <p class="t-display-sm gap-close">
        <span class="gap-close-lead">
          Building an app has never been easier.
        </span>{" "}
        Ube makes growing one just as easy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about-gap {
    padding: 128px 0;
    background: var(--canvas-soft);
    /* Bottom groove only, like the home Problems section — the hero above
       already draws the hairline on this section's top edge. */
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-soft);
  }

  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* --- Statement -------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* Sized in cqi so each row (1.2em tile + 0.36em gap + a 12.6em sentence)
     holds one line up to the 64px cap. */
  .gap-statement {
    --gap-fs: min(64px, 6.8cqi);
    --gap-tile: 1.2em;
    --gap-col: 0.36em;
    /* Tile + gap, in the rows' font size (the close sets its own size). */
    --gap-indent: calc(var(--gap-fs) * 1.56);
    margin-top: 28px;
    container-type: inline-size;
  }
  .gap-title {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--gap-fs);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.12;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .gap-rows {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.36em;
  }
  /* Centring the tile on the line box also centres it on the cap height
     (Inter at a 1.12 line height), and on a two-line sentence centres it
     between the first cap line and the last baseline. */
  .gap-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    column-gap: var(--gap-col);
    align-items: center;
  }
  /* Wraps (balanced) only if a fallback font runs wider than Inter. */
  .gap-line {
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  /* Row one is already true, so it sits a step quieter than the row Ube
     turns: the change should be the brightest line in the section. */
  .gap-row:first-child .gap-line {
    color: var(--body);
  }
  /* The phone layout breaks each sentence after "Anyone can". */
  .gap-br {
    display: none;
  }

  /* --- Tiles ------------------------------------------------------------ */
  /* One em is the tile side, so every piece below is in the icon's own
     proportions. A face is the icon's charcoal (--canvas) surface, set into
     the section's lighter background like an app icon. */
  .gap-tile {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    width: 1em;
    height: 1em;
    font-size: var(--gap-tile);
  }
  .gap-face {
    --t: 0.097em;
    display: block;
    border-radius: 0.23em;
    background: var(--canvas);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--hairline-strong);
  }

  /* Check: an L with the icon's stroke and square ends, turned 45°. */
  .gap-check {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 50%;
    width: 0.46em;
    height: 0.24em;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    border-left: var(--t) solid var(--accent-2);
    border-bottom: var(--t) solid var(--accent-2);
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%) translateY(-0.07em) rotate(-45deg);
  }

  /* The flip card: the Ube icon on the front, the X on the back. At rest
     (and in every fallback) the front faces the reader. */
  .gap-flip {
    transform-style: preserve-3d;
  }
  .gap-flip .gap-face {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    -webkit-backface-visibility: hidden;
    backface-visibility: hidden;
  }
  .gap-face-x {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
  }
  /* X: two bars with the icon's stroke, crossed, in the muted ink. */
  .gap-x::before,
  .gap-x::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 50%;
    width: var(--t);
    height: 0.5em;
    background: var(--muted);
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(45deg);
  }
  .gap-x::after {
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(-45deg);
  }

  /* The lit Ube face: an accent ring plus a soft glow, so it reads as
     switched on next to the plain check tile. */
  .gap-face-ube {
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 1px
        color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 50%, var(--hairline-strong)),
      0 0 0.5em color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 24%, transparent);
  }
  /* Brackets + "u" as one glyph, scaled down for breathing room inside the
     tile. Transform only, so the em-based geometry below is unchanged. */
  .gap-glyph {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    transform: scale(0.78);
  }
  .gap-bracket {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.129em;
    width: 0.135em;
    height: 0.742em;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    border: var(--t) solid var(--accent);
  }
  .gap-bracket-l {
    left: 0.109em;
    border-right: none;
  }
  .gap-bracket-r {
    right: 0.109em;
    border-left: none;
  }
  .gap-u {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
  }
  /* Generated so the heading's text content stays the two sentences. */
  .gap-u::before {
    content: "u";
    font-size: 0.737em;
    /* logo-512.png's stem is ~0.19 of its x-height: Inter Medium. */
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--ink);
    /* Inter's x-height sits below the em box's middle; lift it to centre. */
    transform: translateY(-0.09em);
  }

  /* The strike is a background bar, not text-decoration, so it can be
     erased by animating its size. Sits at Inter's x-height middle. */
  .gap-strike {
    --strike-w: 0.07em;
    background-image: linear-gradient(var(--body), var(--body));
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    background-position: 100% 60%;
    background-size: 0% var(--strike-w);
    -webkit-box-decoration-break: slice;
    box-decoration-break: slice;
  }

  /* --- Close ------------------------------------------------------------ */
  /* Indented to the sentences' text edge, past the tile column, with
     body-like leading for the two lines. */
  .gap-close {
    margin: 72px 0 0;
    padding-left: var(--gap-indent);
    max-width: 680px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink);
    /* Balanced, so the narrow phone column breaks each sentence evenly. */
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  /* The given on its own line, quieter; the answer in ink under it. */
  .gap-close-lead {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    color: var(--body);
  }

  /* --- Motion: the X flips to Ube ------------------------------------- */
  /* Scrubbed by scroll, both ways. Row two arrives showing the X; as it
     rises from ~80% to ~50% down the viewport the card turns over to the
     Ube icon, then the strike erases left to right and the sentence
     brightens. Every keyframe's 100% equals the static rules above, so the
     unsupported and reduced-motion paths need no extra rules. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    @supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
      .gap-row-turn {
        view-timeline: --gap-turn block;
      }
      .gap-flip {
        animation: gap-turn-flip linear both;
      }
      .gap-strike {
        animation: gap-turn-strike linear both;
      }
      .gap-flip,
      .gap-strike {
        animation-timeline: --gap-turn;
        animation-range: cover 20% cover 50%;
      }
    }
  }
  @keyframes gap-turn-flip {
    0%,
    25% {
      transform: perspective(4em) rotateY(180deg);
      animation-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.65, 0, 0.35, 1);
    }
    65%,
    100% {
      transform: perspective(4em) rotateY(0deg);
    }
  }
  @keyframes gap-turn-strike {
    0%,
    55% {
      background-size: 100% var(--strike-w);
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    100% {
      background-size: 0% var(--strike-w);
      color: var(--ink);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .about-gap {
      padding: 96px 0;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .about-gap {
      padding: 72px 0;
    }
    /* Phones: an app-list row. Each sentence breaks after "Anyone can" so
       the words that differ ("build an app." / "acquire users.") line up,
       and the tile grows to the height of the two lines, which keeps the
       turn legible at thumb size. 2em tile + 0.4em gap + 6.7em for
       "acquire users." holds at 10.4cqi down to 320px. */
    .gap-statement {
      --gap-fs: min(44px, 10.4cqi);
      --gap-tile: 2em;
      --gap-col: 0.4em;
      --gap-indent: calc(var(--gap-fs) * 2.4);
      margin-top: 24px;
    }
    .gap-rows {
      gap: 0.5em;
    }
    .gap-br {
      display: inline;
    }
    /* The close steps down to body size so it reads under the two-line
       rows. */
    .gap-close {
      margin-top: 40px;
      font-size: 18px;
    }
  }
</style>
